      - second red hit also turns clockwise
    variant:
      - first red hit spends the only allowed red collision and turns clockwise
      - second red hit sees red quota exhausted, enters the red block, continues straight, and exits at the boundary
    visible_difference:
      - one output branch that existed in the original disappears
      - the beam now forms a straight teal trace up to the exhausted obstacle instead of a second corner
  complexity_calibration:
    - keep the same overall geometry so the task still looks like the source task
    - limit the new numeric parameter to four visible heights because the legend already offers four interior rows
    - force at least one repeated obstacle color encounter in every generated sample, otherwise the quota would be invisible and the sample would collapse back to the original task
  implicit_assumptions_review:
    original_assumptions_that_break:
      - `_parse_legend` assumed one parameter per color and treated the whole colored bar as a direction token
      - the hit handler assumed every obstacle encounter always triggers a turn
      - the oracle generator assumed unlimited repeated turning for the same color
    new_guards:
      - legend parsing now checks that each colored bar is a single vertical column with contiguous bottom-aligned pixels
      - collision handling distinguishes entering an obstacle from already passing through that same obstacle
      - generator validates that capped simulation differs from uncapped simulation on the same grid
  placement_legality:
    - obstacle rectangles are still generated by the original edge-touching span logic, so they remain non-overlapping and solver-friendly
    - penetration is only allowed after a quota is exhausted, and all obstacles touch an edge, so straight-through motion always terminates at the boundary instead of creating long interior ambiguity
    - every generated sample is checked by running the new solver and comparing with the capped oracle output
  visual_observability:
    - the new feature is encoded by visible bar height, not by hidden color ordering or id arithmetic
    - generator requires at least one pass-through event and at least one capped color, so the new behavior changes the output in every accepted sample
    - unused legend colors may still appear, but the main area continues to use 3-4 legend colors as in the source task
  neatness:
