   180	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   181	    """
   182	    Launch four teal beams from a square, with each obstacle color carrying a hook-shaped three-parameter legend rule.
   183	
   184	    Input structure:
   185	    - Top strip: a grey legend split into four black 4x4 cells, each containing one colored hook token.
   186	    - The hook's facing gives left-vs-right handedness, its top-arm size distinguishes 90-degree from 180-degree turns, and its height gives that color's total turning quota.
   187	    - Below the legend is the main area with one solid teal square, a dominant background, and edge-touching colored obstacle rectangles.
   188	
   189	    Rule:
   190	    - Remove the legend from the output.
   191	    - Fire one sz-by-sz teal beam in each cardinal direction from the source square.
   192	    - A beam paints teal only onto background cells while sliding.
   193	    - When a beam first tries to enter obstacle color C and C still has quota left, spend one collision from C and rotate according to that hook: short hooks mean 90-degree left/right turns, long hooks mean 180-degree reversals.
